From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:05:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 131/133] feat(refinery): wire batch merge into
 mol-refinery-patrol behind merge_batch_max=1 (gcp-l8td.10)

merge-batch.sh (select, stack, land, serial; gcp-l8td.8-.11) was inert until the
patrol called it. This wires it in behind a new var, merge_batch_max, default
"1": with the default every rig runs exactly the single-bead lane it ran before,
and batching starts only when a rig sets the var in [rigs.formula_vars]. The
patrol is poured root-only, so the var never rides a pour, and an unrendered
placeholder, an empty value or a non-integer all mean 1.

- find-work: a find-work-batch block follows find-work-query in the same fence
  (the query's text is byte-identical). It truncates the manifest first, reads
  BATCH_MAX with check-inbox's cadence-case shape (INFO, never WARN), and only for
  a head from the assignee scan runs select, writing the 2+ member manifest and
  the script path. A routed-claim head is never batched; a select error is a
  batch of 1.
- rebase: after a clean head rebase, a rebase-batch-stack block runs stack when
  the manifest has 2+ members; a failure removes the manifest. The conflict path
  is unchanged.
- handle-failures: a branch-caused red on a 2+ member manifest runs
  batch-red-serial, which hands the stamping to merge-batch.sh serial (no shell
  logic of its own beyond the member count), rejects nobody and then runs the
  existing pour fence, now wrapped in handle-failures-pour sentinels and
  otherwise untouched. KNOWN and pre-existing reds keep their rules and land the
  batch.
- merge-push: the call becomes land --head "$WORK" for a 2+ member manifest and
  the original merge-push.sh --work line otherwise; the status case is
  unchanged. The prose names the RESULT line's left-open ids and says the next
  iteration's already-merged arm recovers them.

One batch is one iteration: the four session-iteration-stamp blocks and the
one-pour-per-step counts are untouched.

Validation: gastown/tests/test_refinery_batch_wiring.sh (next commit) executes
each block; all 21 gastown suites pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-refinery-patrol.toml | 187 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 184 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-refinery-patrol.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-refinery-patrol.toml
