 case "$MP_STATUS" in
@@ -1006,6 +1175,16 @@ What each status means, and what this step does about it:
 | 11 | `merge_strategy=local` is unsupported: the mayor was mailed. | STOP. Do NOT close the bead, delete the branch or burn the wisp, until a human decides how to proceed. |
 | anything else | Unknown. | STOP and drain. |
 
+With a batch (a manifest of 2+ members) the block ran `merge-batch.sh land`
+instead, and its last output line is `merge-batch: RESULT <status> landed=<ids>
+left-open=<ids>`. Its statuses 0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 mean what the table says and
+this step does what the table says; `land` never returns 4, 9 or 11. Status 0 is
+every member closed. Status 2 after a landing means a member was LANDED but not
+recorded: name each `left-open` id in your patrol-summary, STOP and drain, and
+leave it alone. The next iteration's already-merged arm closes it when it comes
+up as the head. `land` removes the manifest after a landing and cleans up `temp`
+only on 0.
+
 Status 7 is the one that most invites a wrong next move: the remote refused the
 push while `$TARGET` stood still. Re-running the merge immediately just re-runs
 the pre-push gate, so if the gate is saturated the retry is what keeps it
@@ -1024,6 +1203,8 @@ audit trail — the next refinery session can see what happened.
 
 Include:
 - Branch merged (name, target)
+- Batch (if any): the landed and left-open ids from the RESULT line, or the
+  members stamped serial on a red
 - Test results (pass/fail, which checks ran)
 - Bugs filed (IDs, if any pre-existing failures were tracked)
 - Rejections (if the branch was rejected back to pool)
